From bee1824fc54a1acddd3e777069a5c9a4d1121f27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Caleb J. Westfall" <calebwestfall1989@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:27:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] SOTA-2: absolute paths, whole-process-tree CPU budget,
 fail-closed availability gates

Root causes of availability run 42689439284 (all reproduced locally before fixing):
- ProofScope 3/3 NON_ELABORATING and SemantEq 3/3 ERROR: the workflow's relative --out produced
  relative input paths, and tools were started in other working directories ('no such file or
  directory: runs/work/...'). Nothing reached elaboration. All paths are now absolute; a launch check
  returns LAUNCH_ERROR for missing/relative inputs; NON_ELABORATING only when Lean's errors fall inside
  the source declaration, else ADAPTER_ERROR.
- BEq+ 72.1 CPU-s at a 20 CPU-s tier: prlimit --cpu is per process, so every descendant had its own
  budget (4 busy children under a '2 s' limit used 8.04 CPU-s and were reported OK). bench/limits.py now
  enforces the budget on the whole session (+ orphans via child subreaper) by 20 ms polling of
  /proc utime+stime+cutime+cstime, records tree CPU, overshoot, peak tree RSS and processes seen.
  Startup allowance is measured in the availability phase (median of 3 calibration runs, never scored).
- Upstream defaults restored: BEq+ per-proof timeout = upstream DEFAULT_TIMEOUT (was the tier);
  SemantEq keeps its default --timeout (was the tier).
- CI passed with zero usable evaluations: every record now has an evaluation_class; bench/gate.py
  fails the collect job unless each system validly evaluates both equivalent calibration fixtures
  within budget (no verdict required; the non-equivalent fixture is reported, not gated).
- Upstream checks: SemantEq reproduces its own recall-suite manifest on 2 pairs; ProofScope runs its
  v1.2 tests and a Mathlib smoke file; integrity step checks V12 freeze, fixture and JointDrift hashes
  and records competitor pins.

Frozen ProofScope v1.2 files, fixtures, JointDrift, competitor revisions, budgets and labels unchanged.

